# template-backend-go — Cursor project rules

Production Go HTTP microservice template: `chi` router, `log/slog` JSON logging,
OpenTelemetry tracing, graceful shutdown, distroless/static/non-root container.
Go **1.23+**, module `github.com/aircloud/template-backend-go`.

## Commands (use the Makefile)

- `make run` — run locally; `make run-watch` — live reload (air).
- `make test` — `go test -race`; `make cover` — coverage with a 60% gate.
- `make lint` — `golangci-lint run` (strict, `.golangci.yml`); `make format` to fix.
- `make vet`, `make security` (govulncheck + gosec), `make build`, `make docker`.
- `make ci` — full local pipeline; run it before declaring work done.

## Code rules

- Format with `gofumpt` + `goimports`. Comments are full sentences ending with a period.
- Always check errors; wrap with `%w`; use `errors.Is`/`errors.As`.
- Logging: `log/slog` JSON only, **snake_case keys**, context-aware methods in handlers.
- Cap request bodies (`http.MaxBytesReader`), validate input, respond via the helpers in
  `internal/handlers/respond.go`. Keep `internal/httpserver` transport-only.
- No `init()` functions; no new global mutable state. Add tests for behavior changes.

## Security & CI

- Never hardcode secrets; use env vars + `.env.example`. gitleaks runs in CI and pre-commit.
- Keep the container distroless/static/non-root — no shell, no package manager.
- In workflows: pin every action to a 40-hex SHA with a `# vX.Y.Z` comment, start from
  `permissions: contents: read`, set a `concurrency` group, and put `harden-runner` first.
- GHCR/cloud auth is **GitHub OIDC** — never add long-lived secrets or PATs.

## Commits

Conventional Commits, signed (verified). See `CONTRIBUTING.md` and `docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md`.
